<title>FRANCE: MOTOR RACING-FRENCH GRAND PRIX RESULT.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-FRENCH GRAND PRIX RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>MAGNY-COURS, France 1997-06-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of Sunday's</p>
<p>French Grand Prix motor race:</p>
<p>Race distance: 72 laps (305.814 kph)</p>
<p>1. Michael Schumacher (Germany) Ferrari winning time of one</p>
<p>hour, 38 minutes and 50.492 seconds (average speed 185.639 kph)</p>
<p>2. Heinz-Harald Germany) Williams 25.537 seconds behind</p>
<p>3. Eddie Irvine (Britain) Ferrari 1:14.801</p>
<p>4. Jacques Villeneuve (Canada) Williams 1:21.784</p>
<p>5. Jean Alesi (France) Benetton 1:22.735</p>
<p>6. Ralf Schumacher (Germany) Jordan 1:29.871</p>
<p>7. David Coulthard (Britain) McLaren 1 lap</p>
<p>8. Johnny Herbert (Britain) Sauber 1 lap</p>
<p>9. Giancarlo Fisichella (Italy) Jordan 1 lap</p>
<p>10. Jarno Trulli (Italy) Prost 2 laps</p>
<p>11. Ukyo Katayama (Japan) Minardi 2 laps</p>
<p>12. Damon Hill (Britain) Arrows 3 laps</p>
<p>Not classified (did not finish):</p>
<p>13. Mika Salo (Finland) Tyrrell 61 laps completed</p>
<p>14. Alexander Wurz (Austria) Benetton 60</p>
<p>15. Pedro Diniz (Brazil) Arrows 58</p>
<p>16. Norberto Fontana (Argentina) Sauber 40</p>
<p>17. Rubens Barrichello (Brazil) Stewart 36</p>
<p>18. Jan Magnussen (Denmark) Stewart 33</p>
<p>19. Mika Hakkinen (Finland) McLaren 18</p>
<p>20. Jos Verstappen (Netherlands) Tyrrell 15</p>
<p>21. Shinji Nakano (Japan) Prost 7</p>
<p>22. Tarso Marques (Brazil) Minardi 5</p>
<p>Fastest lap: Schumacher 1:17.910 (196.380)</p>
</text>
